'<p class="l-text"><strong>Random number generation, file I/O, and real-world integration</strong> are the skills that turn NumPy from a learning exercise into a production tool. This final lesson covers the modern random API, probability distributions, Monte Carlo simulations, data persistence, Matplotlib integration, and a complete ML pipeline built entirely with NumPy.</p>'

+ '<div class="calc-highlight"><strong>Why this matters:</strong> Every ML experiment starts with random initialization, every dataset lives on disk, and every result needs visualization. Mastering these practical tools means you can go from raw data to trained model without leaving NumPy.</div>'
