+ '<div class="calc-graph"><div class="graph-caption"><strong>What this graph shows:</strong> Three fundamental distributions overlaid. The Normal (green) is the classic bell curve centered at 0. Uniform (red) has constant density between 0 and 4. Exponential (blue) decays rapidly \u2014 most values are near zero. These shapes define the probability of drawing any particular value.</div></div>'

